*.safetensors

# EXCEPTION: the trained LoRA adapter must be committed or Stage 2 is not reproducible.
# The clean-clone test caught this — a stranger got adapter_config.json (963 B) but no weights,
# so the adapter could not be loaded and the whole three-arm comparison was unrunnable.
# 26.6 MB, which is fine for git. The 200/400/600/800 training checkpoints stay ignored:
# they are 26.6 MB each and are only needed to re-examine checkpoint choice, not to reproduce.
!results/adapters/*/adapters.safetensors
*.gguf
mlx_model/
m-fp16/
m-int8/
m-int4/
.venv/
__pycache__/
corpus/*.pdf
# NEVER commit the plaintext key or the Fernet secret.
# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing-comment syntax — a line like
#   answer_key.json      # NEVER commit plaintext key
# is read as a pattern containing the spaces and the '#', so it matches nothing
# and the file stays committable. Comments must be on their own line.
# (The build spec's .gitignore snippet has exactly that bug; `git check-ignore -v`
# confirmed both files were unignored before this fix.)
answer_key.json
.answer_key_secret
*.faiss
index/
